% Test cases for the manual wheelchair policy (manual_wheelchairs.le):
% synthetic claims, one or two per criterion of LCD L33788 and per payment
% condition of Policy Article A52497. Findings are recorded as the treating
% practitioner's (the face-to-face note), the supplier's (the home
% assessment) or the Council's; a finding nobody made leaves the answer
% conditional. The queries: whether the claim is payable (the first query,
% so "stage" reads its checklist), whether it is reasonable and necessary,
% and what minimal change would make it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base manual wheelchairs cases includes these resources:
    manual_wheelchairs.

the knowledge base manual wheelchairs cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete ultralightweight wheelchair (K0005) file: the general criteria
% A–E and F, the ultralightweight criteria (a full-time user, the specialty
% evaluation, the ATP), the face-to-face encounter, the order communicated
% before delivery, the prior authorization (K0005 is on both lists),
% delivery with proof, the home assessment and the K0005 documentation.
scenario ultralightweight_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the ultralightweight wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the ultralightweight wheelchair is "K0005".
    the ultralightweight wheelchair is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-04-10.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates manual wheelchair about Ann is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding manual wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use manual wheelchair at home about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair can be propelled about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "sufficient upper extremity function to self-propel during a typical day".
    the finding ultralightweight wheelchair justified about Ann is established, according to the physical therapist, because "a full-time manual wheelchair user".
    Ann had a specialty evaluation by a licensed medical professional with no financial relationship with the supplier for the ultralightweight wheelchair.
    a RESNA certified assistive technology professional employed by the supplier was directly involved in the selection of the ultralightweight wheelchair.
    the treating practitioner examined Ann for the ultralightweight wheelchair in a face-to-face encounter on 2026-02-01.
    the order for the ultralightweight wheelchair is dated 2026-02-15.
    the order for the ultralightweight wheelchair is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the ultralightweight wheelchair includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the ultralightweight wheelchair includes order date.
    the order for the ultralightweight wheelchair includes description of the item.
    the order for the ultralightweight wheelchair includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the ultralightweight wheelchair includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the ultralightweight wheelchair was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-16.
    prior authorization for the ultralightweight wheelchair was affirmed on 2026-03-01.
    the ultralightweight wheelchair was delivered on 2026-04-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the ultralightweight wheelchair.
    the home assessment for the ultralightweight wheelchair is documented.
    the medical record describes the routine activities of Ann.
    the written report of the specialty evaluation for the ultralightweight wheelchair is available.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% A complete standard wheelchair (K0001) file: K0001 is on neither list, so
% no face-to-face encounter or prior authorization is needed; the order
% reached the supplier before the date of service.
scenario standard_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the standard wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the standard wheelchair is "K0001".
    the standard wheelchair is furnished to Ben.
    the residence of Ben is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates manual wheelchair about Ben is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding manual wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use manual wheelchair at home about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair can be propelled about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "the daughter who lives with him is available, willing and able to push the wheelchair".
    the order for the standard wheelchair is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the standard wheelchair is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the standard wheelchair includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the standard wheelchair includes order date.
    the order for the standard wheelchair includes description of the item.
    the order for the standard wheelchair includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the standard wheelchair includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the standard wheelchair was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the standard wheelchair was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the standard wheelchair.
    the home assessment for the standard wheelchair is documented.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% The Council finds the record does not show that a cane or walker would not
% do (criterion B): the claim is not reasonable and necessary.
scenario walking_aids_unsupported is:
    claim 1 is for the standard wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the standard wheelchair is "K0001".
    the standard wheelchair is furnished to Cy.
    the residence of Cy is private residence.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Cy is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the record shows the beneficiary ambulating with a walker".
    the finding home accommodates manual wheelchair about Cy is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding manual wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use manual wheelchair at home about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair can be propelled about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% Nobody has found that the beneficiary can propel the wheelchair or has a
% caregiver who can (criterion F or G): the answer is conditional on that
% finding.
scenario propulsion_not_found is:
    claim 1 is for the standard wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the standard wheelchair is "K0001".
    the standard wheelchair is furnished to Dee.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates manual wheelchair about Dee is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding manual wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use manual wheelchair at home about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding manual wheelchair can be propelled about Dee is established"].

% A hemi-wheelchair (K0002) for a beneficiary of short stature who needs a
% lower seat height, and one (claim 2) for a beneficiary whose record does
% not say so.
scenario hemi is:
    claim 1 is for the hemi wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the hemi wheelchair is "K0002".
    the hemi wheelchair is furnished to Eve.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates manual wheelchair about Eve is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding manual wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use manual wheelchair at home about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair can be propelled about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding lower seat height required about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "short stature".
    claim 2 is for the other hemi wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the other hemi wheelchair is "K0002".
    the other hemi wheelchair is furnished to Fay.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates manual wheelchair about Fay is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding manual wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use manual wheelchair at home about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair can be propelled about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding lower seat height required about Fay is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the record does not state the beneficiary's height or that the feet are used for propulsion".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A lightweight wheelchair (K0003): the beneficiary cannot self-propel a
% standard wheelchair and can and does self-propel a lightweight one.
scenario lightweight is:
    claim 1 is for the lightweight wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the lightweight wheelchair is "K0003".
    the lightweight wheelchair is furnished to Gus.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates manual wheelchair about Gus is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding manual wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use manual wheelchair at home about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair can be propelled about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding standard wheelchair not self propellable about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "limited endurance".
    the finding self propels lightweight wheelchair about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The same lightweight wheelchair where the Council finds the beneficiary
% self-propels a standard wheelchair: criterion (1) fails.
scenario lightweight_standard_would_do is:
    claim 1 is for the lightweight wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the lightweight wheelchair is "K0003".
    the lightweight wheelchair is furnished to Gus.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates manual wheelchair about Gus is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding manual wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use manual wheelchair at home about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair can be propelled about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding standard wheelchair not self propellable about Gus is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the therapy notes record the beneficiary propelling a standard wheelchair through the home".
    the finding self propels lightweight wheelchair about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].

% A high strength lightweight wheelchair (K0004): claim 1 for a two-month
% post-operative need is not reasonable and necessary; claim 2, for a
% twelve-month need, is.
scenario high_strength_lightweight_duration is:
    claim 1 is for the short term wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the short term wheelchair is "K0004".
    the short term wheelchair is furnished to Hal.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the expected duration of need for the short term wheelchair is 2 months.
    claim 2 is for the long term wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the long term wheelchair is "K0004".
    the long term wheelchair is furnished to Hal.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the expected duration of need for the long term wheelchair is 12 months.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates manual wheelchair about Hal is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding manual wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use manual wheelchair at home about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair can be propelled about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding high strength lightweight wheelchair justified about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "self-propels while engaging in frequent activities in the home that cannot be performed in a standard or lightweight wheelchair".
    rn expects answers ["claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

