% Weight: a 280-pound beneficiary is over the 250 pounds of the heavy duty
% wheelchair (K0006, claim 1) but not over the 300 pounds of the extra heavy
% duty wheelchair (K0007, claim 2).
scenario weight_class is:
    claim 1 is for the heavy duty wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the heavy duty wheelchair is "K0006".
    the heavy duty wheelchair is furnished to Ivy.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    claim 2 is for the extra heavy duty wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the extra heavy duty wheelchair is "K0007".
    the extra heavy duty wheelchair is furnished to Ivy.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Ivy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Ivy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates manual wheelchair about Ivy is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding manual wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Ivy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use manual wheelchair at home about Ivy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair can be propelled about Ivy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the weight of Ivy is 280 pounds.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A heavy duty wheelchair (K0006) for a 200-pound beneficiary with severe
% spasticity: the alternative ground.
scenario heavy_duty_spasticity is:
    claim 1 is for the heavy duty wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the heavy duty wheelchair is "K0006".
    the heavy duty wheelchair is furnished to Jon.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Jon is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Jon is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates manual wheelchair about Jon is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding manual wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Jon is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use manual wheelchair at home about Jon is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair can be propelled about Jon is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the weight of Jon is 200 pounds.
    the medical record of Jon documents severe spasticity.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A tilt-in-space wheelchair (E1161): the general criteria, the specialty
% evaluation and the ATP.
scenario tilt_in_space is:
    claim 1 is for the tilt in space wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the tilt in space wheelchair is "E1161".
    the tilt in space wheelchair is furnished to Kim.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Kim is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Kim is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates manual wheelchair about Kim is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding manual wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Kim is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use manual wheelchair at home about Kim is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair can be propelled about Kim is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "the spouse is available, willing and able to assist".
    Kim had a specialty evaluation by a licensed medical professional with no financial relationship with the supplier for the tilt in space wheelchair.
    a RESNA certified assistive technology professional employed by the supplier was directly involved in the selection of the tilt in space wheelchair.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A transport chair (E1037): criteria A–E and G, the caregiver.
scenario transport_chair is:
    claim 1 is for the transport chair.
    the HCPCS code of the transport chair is "E1037".
    the transport chair is furnished to Lou.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Lou is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Lou is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates manual wheelchair about Lou is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding manual wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Lou is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use manual wheelchair at home about Lou is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding caregiver available for manual wheelchair about Lou is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "the son lives with the beneficiary and pushes the chair".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A custom manual wheelchair base (K0008) for a six-month need, and a
% pediatric size base (E1231) on the general criteria.
scenario custom_and_pediatric is:
    claim 1 is for the custom base.
    the HCPCS code of the custom base is "K0008".
    the custom base is furnished to Max.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the expected duration of need for the custom base is 6 months.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Max is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Max is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates manual wheelchair about Max is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding manual wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Max is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use manual wheelchair at home about Max is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair can be propelled about Max is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding custom manual wheelchair base required about Max is established, according to the physical therapist, because "no standard base with seating systems, cushions, options or accessories fits the fixed pelvic obliquity".
    claim 2 is for the pediatric wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the pediatric wheelchair is "E1231".
    the pediatric wheelchair is furnished to Nia.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Nia is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Nia is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates manual wheelchair about Nia is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding manual wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Nia is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use manual wheelchair at home about Nia is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair can be propelled about Nia is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "the mother pushes the chair".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

% One month's rental of a standard wheelchair (K0001) while the
% beneficiary's own wheelchair is repaired: covered on that ground alone
% (the second answer is the general path, conditional on the six findings
% nobody has recorded).
scenario loaner_during_repair is:
    claim 1 is for the loaner wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the loaner wheelchair is "K0001".
    the loaner wheelchair is furnished to Ola.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Ola owns a wheelchair that is being repaired.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding significant mobility limitation about Ola is established", "the finding walking aids insufficient about Ola is established", "the finding home accommodates manual wheelchair about Ola is established", "the finding manual wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Ola is established", "the finding willing to use manual wheelchair at home about Ola is established", "the finding manual wheelchair can be propelled about Ola is established"].

% Reasonable and necessary, but the home assessment is not documented
% (Policy Article A52497): payable fails at the remedy.
scenario no_home_assessment is:
    claim 1 is for the standard wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the standard wheelchair is "K0001".
    the standard wheelchair is furnished to Ben.
    the residence of Ben is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates manual wheelchair about Ben is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding manual wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use manual wheelchair at home about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair can be propelled about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the order for the standard wheelchair is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the standard wheelchair is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the standard wheelchair includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the standard wheelchair includes order date.
    the order for the standard wheelchair includes description of the item.
    the order for the standard wheelchair includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the standard wheelchair includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the standard wheelchair was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the standard wheelchair was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the standard wheelchair.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the home assessment for the standard wheelchair is documented"]].

